WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.510
Messages organizes departmental notices into Inbox, Sent, and All Messages.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.640
Chat organizes ongoing conversations.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.229
Choose the audience and purpose before composing anything.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.549
Community response teams can use a notice for a briefing and a chat for

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:21.170
coordination; industrial teams can use the same distinction for shift handovers.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.549
A stored message in your own app confirms a record, not delivery

00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:27.260
to every recipient’s device.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.000
The Compose icon

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.880
opens New Message.

00:00:30.309 --> 00:00:35.179
Choose Message Type and Recipients, then enter a clear Subject and Message Body.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.009
The recipient picker separates People, Groups, and Roles.

00:00:39.389 --> 00:00:41.469
Check the selected names before Send.

00:00:41.929 --> 00:00:45.069
Our training notice goes only to the fictional Boden account.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.130
Find its saved card in Sent and open the content afterward; do not treat that

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.280
card as proof of a push notification.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.419
An incoming Poll can open Respond to Message through its reply arrow.

00:00:56.869 --> 00:00:58.000
Enter Response,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
add a Note (Optional),

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.589
and choose Send Response.

00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:05.360
The training polls show a stored Yes response as code one;

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.479
inspect the Responded result.

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:11.309
Long-pressing a card exposes Select All and Delete.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.379
Review the selection carefully.

00:01:13.779 --> 00:01:17.690
This browser’s native confirmation does not complete deletion, so these

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.729
examples preserve both messages.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:24.870
Open New conversation and choose New Direct Message for one person or

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:26.870
New Group for a shared discussion.

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:30.459
Search for the intended member instead of choosing Everyone.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:34.680
Name the group and review the selected people before you create the group.

00:01:35.029 --> 00:01:39.040
Direct messages, channels, and incidents then organize the list.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:44.390
SAR task teams and security posts can use these same audience checks to avoid

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.469
sending coordination to the wrong team.

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:50.520
Confirm the conversation name before entering Type a message.

00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:53.000
Attach is the plus icon;

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.870
its menu offers Emoji, Add image, Add GIF, Share

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.150
location, and Urgent in a channel.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.980
Send is the paper-plane icon and becomes available after entering text.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:06.670
Threads offer fewer attachment choices.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.799
This exercise uses fictional text; media services, location permissions,

00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:15.519
and real hardware require separate checks on the intended platform.

00:02:15.789 --> 00:02:18.289
Long-press a message to inspect its actions.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.089
The training account’s own-message menu shows Reply in thread, Copy, Edit,

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:27.400
Delete, Pin, and moderator removal.

00:02:27.789 --> 00:02:30.879
Available actions depend on ownership and permissions.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.440
Thread keeps the ORIGINAL MESSAGE visible while you add related replies.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:39.720
Review the target before editing, pinning, deleting, or moderating.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.729
The captured reply is fictional; no deletion or moderator

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.149
removal is demonstrated.

00:02:45.309 --> 00:02:49.810
Assistant opens a question workspace with New session and a Send icon.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.849
Decide what you need to know and whether the information is approved for that

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:56.009
service before submitting anything.

00:02:56.469 --> 00:02:59.870
A bounded question about a training procedure is more useful than

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.550
a vague request for everything.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.249
This recording stays on the workspace: it does not invoke a

00:03:05.249 --> 00:03:07.290
provider or validate an answer.

00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:11.550
Verify any operational answer against approved references.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.680
Voice opens Voice Channels.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:18.129
This training configuration says No voice channels available, so

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:19.850
there is no channel to join here.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.430
Resolve that setup before relying on voice coordination.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.090
A configured deployment also needs the intended device’s audio permissions,

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.069
microphone, and push-to-talk equipment checked through an approved test.

00:03:32.399 --> 00:03:37.249
An empty browser list cannot establish native radio or background-audio behavior.

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:40.559
Keep the team’s agreed fallback communication available.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.479
Stream opens Audio Streams and Select Audio Stream.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.390
None means no stream is selected; the screen also says no audio

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.799
stream is currently playing.

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:53.930
Refresh Streams reloads the configured list.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:58.599
In Settings, BT Handset currently says No device selected.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.670
Inspect these states before troubleshooting audio.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:06.280
Browser settings do not demonstrate Bluetooth pairing, headset buttons, or

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:10.890
native background playback, and this exercise does not connect a real provider.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:14.760
Contacts opens Contact Details with Details, Notes,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.139
Pre-Plan, Files, and Calls.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:21.000
Confirm the contact’s identity before following its information.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:25.550
Our fictional warehouse has no recorded preplan, notes, files,

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.419
or related calls in these tabs.

00:04:27.769 --> 00:04:31.410
That absence does not establish that the site has no hazards.

00:04:31.629 --> 00:04:35.829
Wildland and industrial teams can use the same tabs for reliable access

00:04:35.829 --> 00:04:39.679
information and site documents once their department has populated them.

00:04:39.869 --> 00:04:43.359
Notes contains the Firehouse 51 — shift briefing.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:47.890
Open it to read the actual briefing content and its category and date.

00:04:48.369 --> 00:04:52.209
Protocols is a separate reference library; this training department

00:04:52.209 --> 00:04:53.890
shows No protocols found.

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:57.940
Search the appropriate library and confirm that an approved reference

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.790
exists before relying on it.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.549
Reading a briefing does not create a protocol, and an empty

00:05:03.549 --> 00:05:07.389
library is a reason to obtain the correct departmental material.

00:05:07.629 --> 00:05:12.460
In Settings, inspect Keep Alive, Realtime Geolocation, Background

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.940
Geolocation, and BT Handset.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:19.700
These preferences affect different device capabilities; do not assume

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.049
one switch enables all field behavior.

00:05:22.429 --> 00:05:26.450
Native background location, audio hardware, and push notifications

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:31.030
require the appropriate platform, permissions, and an approved device test.

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:34.540
This browser exercise leaves the location switches off.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.550
Confirm actual alert receipt separately before a team depends

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.350
on a device for notifications.
